3
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.640 line:88% position:50% size:90%
Swallowing has four phases.

4
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.780 line:88% position:50% size:90%
Oral preparation forms a bolus.

5
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.990 line:88% position:50% size:90%
Oral transit moves that bolus toward the

6
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.650 line:88% position:50% size:90%
back of the mouth.

7
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.230 line:88% position:50% size:90%
During the pharyngeal phase, the soft palate

8
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.690 line:88% position:50% size:90%
closes off the nasal route, the larynx

9
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.290 line:88% position:50% size:90%
rises, and several airway protections work
together

10
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.420 line:88% position:50% size:90%
while the bolus enters the esophagus.

11
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.330 line:88% position:50% size:90%
Esophageal transport then carries it toward
the

12
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:23.990 line:88% position:50% size:90%
stomach.

13
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.190 line:88% position:50% size:90%
This is a slowed schematic of coordinated

14
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.550 line:88% position:50% size:90%
events, not four steps that last the

15
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.320 line:88% position:50% size:90%
same amount of time.

16
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.280 line:88% position:50% size:90%
Development changes the feeding task.

17
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.390 line:88% position:50% size:90%
An infant's sucking pattern is not the

18
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.290 line:88% position:50% size:90%
same skill as a toddler bringing a

19
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.100 line:88% position:50% size:90%
